VERDICT: the TEC is not sensitive enough to weigh one heater at a safe voltage.
Measured sensitivity 0.147 mV/mW (5.18 mV at 9.4 mW to 15.63 mV at 80.4 mW), against a
between-dwell noise floor of 3.34 mV after averaging 30 s per dwell to beat the loop's 4.5 s
limit cycle. An unknown channel staged at 1.5 V dissipates ~20 mW and so produces ~2.9 mV --
SNR below 1. Reaching the 5 sigma gate needs ~114 mW, i.e. 3.6 V on a channel whose current
rating cannot be checked, which is the thing the measurement was for.

The substitution method itself is sound and its self-test recovers known resistances to 2.15%
against a simulated calorimeter; the instrument is what fails, not the maths. Use an ohmmeter:
UH6 = TP11/TP10, UH14 = TP26/TP25, UH18 = TP26/BP21 (mrunal/PIC1A_packaged_IO.pdf p.5).
